# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW THE RULES BELOW ARE WRITTEN
#
# Every rule here is anchored or scoped to where the thing it excludes
# actually lives. That is not tidiness -- an unanchored rule matches at every
# depth, and this file has already silently eaten three sets of source files
# that way:
#
#   world/  ate  mods/transformers/src/main/java/fiskfille/tf/common/world/
#   *.ogg   ate  the Transformers mod's 19 shipped sound effects, and the
#                menu music, while the sounds.json naming them stayed tracked
#
# Nothing failed. The mod compiled, loaded, and ran silently mute; the only
# symptom was a 630 KB shortfall in the jar. A clean checkout could not build
# a complete pack, and nothing said so.
#
# So: anchor directory rules with a leading or embedded "/", scope extension
# rules to the tree that generates them, and leave the source-tree guard at
# the bottom of this file in place.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
bin/
.gradle/
gradle-app.setting
tools/**/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradle dev-client runtime. Recreated by `./gradlew runClient`; never source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
run/
logs/
crash-reports/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party binaries.
#
# This repository holds the pack's *source*: the mods we author, the config
# that defines the pack, the tools that build its assets. It deliberately does
# not redistribute other people's mod jars, the Minecraft or Forge jars, or the
# libraries they depend on. pack/mods.tsv records exactly which versions the
# pack loads; see docs/setup/install-on-mac.md for where they come from.
#
# mods/transformers/libs/ is four of those: NEI, CodeChickenLib,
# CodeChickenCore and Waila, staged out of the live instance because the mod
# compiles against the exact jars the pack loads. They are not committed;
# `tools/stage_transformers_libs.py` copies them in from a live instance. See
# that script and docs/development/building-on-windows.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jar
*.zip
# ...except the Gradle wrappers, without which a fresh clone cannot build.
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated renders. Every one of these is reproducible from the generator
# beside it in tools/ -- see tools/README.md.
#
# SCOPED TO tools/ ON PURPOSE. Audio that ships inside a mod or the
# resourcepack is source, is not reproducible from anything in this repo, and
# must stay tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/**/*.wav
tools/**/*.aiff
tools/**/*.mp3
tools/**/*.ogg
tools/**/work/
tools/**/_work/
tools/**/backups/
tools/**/backup-before/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Worlds and player data. Large, binary, and personal.
#
# ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. Unanchored, "world/" matches any directory named
# world at any depth, including Java packages -- which is exactly how
# fiskfille.tf.common.world went missing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/saves/
/world/
server/runtime/
pack/**/saves/
*.mca
*.dat_old
usercache.json
usernamecache.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc snapshots. This is what version control is for -- commit instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.pre-*
*-20[0-9][0-9][0-1][0-9][0-3][0-9]*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOURCE-TREE GUARD -- keep this last.
#
# Nothing generated lives in a mod's src/ or in pack/resourcepack/. Everything
# there is authored and must be tracked, whatever its extension. These
# negations are a safety net for a future over-broad rule above, so the next
# one costs a `git status` line instead of a silently incomplete build.
#
# The net has a hard limit git imposes: a negation CANNOT resurrect a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded. It rescues file-pattern rules (*.ogg)
# only. Directory rules must be anchored correctly in the first place -- so if
# you add one, anchor it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!mods/*/src/**
!pack/resourcepack/**
# ...but a stray build artefact inside a source tree is still not source.
mods/*/src/**/*.class
